# Audio Amplifier PCB

A low-power audio amplifier PCB designed using the LM386 audio amplifier IC.  
This board amplifies a low-level audio signal to drive a small speaker or external audio load.

## Overview
The design focuses on simplicity, clean signal routing, and ease of assembly using through-hole components. It includes adjustable gain and proper input/output coupling to ensure stable audio performance.

## Key Features
- LM386-based audio amplifier
- Adjustable gain using a potentiometer
- AC-coupled input and output
- Operates on a 12 V DC supply
- Screw terminals for audio input and output

## Design Highlights
- Input coupling capacitor to block DC offsets
- External gain control network
- Output decoupling for load protection
- Compact single-layer PCB layout

## Files Included
- Audio Amplifier.kicad_sch – Schematic
- Audio Amplifier.kicad_pcb – PCB layout
